# Expectation record for 01_integer_conversions/003_signed_unsigned_comparison.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 003_signed_unsigned_comparison
area               = 01_integer_conversions
description        = Comparisons across signedness where the common type decides the result, folded and volatile-runtime
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
A bare implicit signed/unsigned comparison is rejected by -Wsign-compare, which -Wextra
supplies and this program's gate keeps, so every comparison either promotes the mismatch
away, uses a provably non-negative signed operand, converts explicitly, or sits in an
unevaluated _Generic controlling expression.  No conversion to an unsigned type is applied
to a negative value except where the modular result is the property under test and is
written explicitly.  Every property is computed twice, once from literal constants and once from
volatile-qualified storage, so the constant folder's answer cannot stand in for the
one the backend computes at run time.
No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a
standard-library header bcc does not ship.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
fold_lt_ushort=1
fold_lt_uchar=1
fold_lt_llong_uint=1
fold_gt_ullong=1
fold_lt_int_uint=0
fold_eq_int_uint=1
fold_uac_sensitive=1
run_lt_ushort=1
run_lt_uchar=1
run_lt_llong_uint=1
run_gt_ullong=1
run_lt_int_uint=0
run_eq_int_uint=1
run_uac_sensitive=1
common_int_uint=unsigned int
common_llong_uint=long long
common_llong_ullong=unsigned long long
END
